## Epic scope (what “external actions” ultimately includes)

| Track | Contents |
|-------|-----------|
| **Slice 1 (spec below)** | Monthly **consultant-issued** invoice (**`supplier-issued` + `invoice_cadence: monthly`** in data): domain occupancy + gap guards, preview/commit workflow and fingerprint, Resend (**or**) adapter hook, persisted outbox, outcome MCP tools (**`preview_monthly_invoice`** / **`commit_monthly_invoice`**) and **matching HTTP endpoints** consumed by **`public/src/modules/invoices.ts`**. Natural inputs: **`client_name`** resolution server-side (`legal_name` / `trading_name`), **`billing_month` optional with default policy (e.g. previous complete calendar month)**. UI must not reimplement occupancy rules once preview returns **`occupancy`/`flags`** from the brain. |
| **Later slices** | Accountant artefact bundles (VAT / CT / SA) with manifests + validation; broader approval UX; structured audit trail; parity tools that stay outcome-named where assistants should not compose raw HTTP chains. |

The epic **does not** map 1:1 to existing REST; it **extends** Hermes/UI after parity.

